WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.454 --> 00:00:04.963
(birds chirping)

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:07.713
(chain clanging)

00:00:09.191 --> 00:00:12.024
(uplifting guitar music)

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.790
- This is pretty close
to a perfect morning.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.893
We got a beautiful sunrise coming up here.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.773
That's beautiful, heavenly.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.310
And the cows think so as well.

00:00:28.336 --> 00:00:31.063
(laughs) They're liking that grass.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.970
It's cold today and windy,

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.050
and so I wanted to get
this baby calf picked up

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.624
and brought him in here where
it'd be nice and warm and dry.

00:00:49.624 --> 00:00:51.033
Here you go little feller.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.880
As you can see, these
cows mean a lot to me.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.180
When I was growing up as a kid,

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.310
I was assigned to take
care of the baby calves.

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:01.620
And I learned how to love
'em and how to care for 'em.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.623
I think they feel love just
as much as any one of us do.

00:01:04.623 --> 00:01:07.206
(gentle music)

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.760
The cow is what she eats.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.540
In order to have the high
quality, great-tasting milk,

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.290
we gotta have her eating high quality,

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.530
great-tasting food as well.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.360
Cows are kind of like any one of us.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.710
They've got likes and dislikes,

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:23.290
and they're not afraid
to voice their opinion

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.066
by mooing at ya.

00:01:25.066 --> 00:01:27.566
(cows mooing)

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:31.120
Cows naturally love to eat grass.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:33.060
That'd be their number one choice.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:34.260
When our soil is healthy,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.150
that's what creates the right
quality of crop for the cows.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.520
We strive to plant the pasture

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:41.180
with a variety of different
species in their grass

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.120
to create biodiversity.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.870
These legumes, or clovers,

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.870
they offer different types
of nutrients to the cows.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.990
Each one of these plants
pulls carbon dioxide

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:54.943
out of the atmosphere and places
it into the soil as carbon.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:58.590
You'll notice, as these
cows are walking around,

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.870
they're releasing their
manure across the grass,

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.840
and the cows will stomp
this down into the soil,

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.540
and this'll become a nutrient source.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:08.340
Within the soil is a little
ecosystem all of its own.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.160
There's all sorts of little
organisms that live in there.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.573
And if I mistreat my ground,
then the soil will be depleted.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.480
Horizon Organic supports family farms

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.550
by helping us have the
know-how that we need

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:23.890
to ensure that our soil
is being protected,

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:26.620
and to be able to market our
milk throughout the country.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.090
We all have the same goal,

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.940
to produce the very best milk possible.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.050
I take great pride in my family farm.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:34.960
Millions of people expect
me to take good care

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.160
of my animals and my crops,

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:39.320
so that they have clean,
healthy food to eat every day.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.998
You wanna be a farmer Hoss?

00:02:40.998 --> 00:02:41.831
- [Hoss] Mm-hmm.

00:02:41.831 --> 00:02:44.164
- What about you Stagger,
you wanna drive big tractors?

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:44.997
- Mm-hmm.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.650
- [Cody] One thing that is
everlasting is the soil.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:50.150
I'm farming the soil that my grandpa,

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.400
my great-grandpa, my dad farmed.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.720
And it brings me a huge amount of joy

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.553
to not only myself, but my family.

